  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5607.04 Express Consent",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5607.04 Express Consent.\n\n(a) Unless a person gives their express consent, the department shall not release motor vehicle records for the purposes specified in RSA 260:14, V(a)(8) and (9).\n\n(b) Express consent may be given by submitting in writing to the department a letter including the following information:\n\n(1) The person's name, address, and date of birth;\n\n(2) The motor vehicle record information that the department may release;\n\n(3) A statement that the person gives their express consent to the release of their motor vehicle record information for purposes specified in RSA 260:14, V(a)(8) and (9).\n\n(c) Once received, a letter giving a person's express consent to release of motor vehicle records shall remain in effect for two years. Nothing shall prevent the person from withdrawing his or her express consent at any time.\n\nSource. #7361, EXEMPT, eff 9-1-00; ss by #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
